WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:05.370
We're just a month away from the premiere
of Frozen II, and fans can't wait to see what

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:08.180
unfolds in the sequel to the beloved Disney
film.

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:13.280
Audiences are especially hopeful that the
film will finally reveal something many of

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:16.700
us have been wondering since Frozen was released
in 2013.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:22.340
King Agnarr and Queen Iduna of Arendelle played
a small, but critical, role in Frozen.

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:27.150
At the beginning of the film, they hide a
young Elsa away in an attempt to control her

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:29.480
powers, putting a wedge between her and Anna.

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:34.260
Just a few scenes into the movie, they board
a ship, leaving their now-grown daughters

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:35.200
in Arendelle.

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:40.059
They're shipwrecked after being caught in
a storm, and the crown falls to Elsa.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:45.880
Now, if Frozen II remains true to Disney formula
— which seems to, with few exceptions, leave

00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:51.170
its protagonists either orphaned or with one
living parent — then Elsa and Anna's parents

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:51.800
are dead.

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:55.960
The Frozen II trailer that dropped in June,
however, makes us think that things might

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:57.700
be headed in another direction.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.320
The trailer opens with Elsa growing into her
powers, battling tidal waves.

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:07.180
Underwater, she encounters a mythical Norse
water spirit called a Nokk.

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:12.500
Elsa and Anna then embark on a quest, urged
on by the troll Grand Pabbie who delivers

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:13.960
an ominous warning:

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:15.500
"Elsa.

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:19.600
The past is not what it seems."

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:22.760
We also see Queen Iduna in trailer footage.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:28.240
Some fans have taken all of this to mean that
one or both of Elsa and Anna's parents are

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:33.460
still alive, and that one of them may have
powers of their own that enabled them to survive

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:34.360
the shipwreck.

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:39.040
There's also speculation that the water horse
was sent as a message to Elsa and Anna, to

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:41.660
tell them that the shipwreck hadn't been fatal.

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:45.640
This ties into other fan theories that came
out after Frozen's release.

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:50.880
One such theory speculates that Elsa and Anna's
parents might also be Tarzan's parents.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:56.500
While the man and woman in Tarzan don't really
look like King Agnarr and Queen Iduna, Tarzan's

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:59.660
parents did end up stranded following a shipwreck.

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:03.800
Even Frozen's director, Chris Buck, said that
he likes this theory.

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:07.560
In Buck's imagination, King Agnarr and Queen
Iduna don't die.

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:10.190
He told MTV News that in his mind:

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:15.160
"They get shipwrecked, and somehow they really
washed way far away from the Scandinavian

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:17.040
waters, and they end up in the jungle.

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:21.700
They end up building a tree house and a leopard
kills them, so their baby boy is raised by

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:22.440
gorillas."

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:23.720
He also added:

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:28.780
"So in my little head, Anna and Elsa's brother
is Tarzan — but on the other side of that

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:32.820
island are surfing penguins, to tie in a non-Disney
movie, Surf's Up.

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:34.700
That's my fun little world."

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:39.500
Another favorite fan theory connects Elsa
and Anna's parents to The Little Mermaid and

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:40.360
Tangled.

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:45.200
Could the sunken ship we see in The Little
Mermaid actually belong to King Agnarr and

00:02:45.209 --> 00:02:46.209
Queen Iduna?

00:02:46.209 --> 00:02:50.630
According to this theory, Elsa and Anna's
parents were on their way to Rapunzel and

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:55.080
Flynn's wedding when their ship crashed, leaving
it for Ariel to one day explore.

00:02:55.380 --> 00:03:00.060
From there, Rapunzel and Flynn feel guilty
for the deaths of Elsa and Anna's parents,

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:03.600
leading them to attend Elsa's coronation three
years later.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:08.760
It's not a lot to go on, but the theories
and the trailer do give us some hope that

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:11.880
Elsa and Anna's parents survived the terrible
shipwreck.

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:17.040
Will Frozen II see the king and queen reunited
with Elsa and Anna, giving them a chance to

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:19.800
be a happy family with no more secrets between
them?

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:25.480
It's true that Disney has a habit of making
its princesses orphans, but Disney films are

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:27.800
even better known for their happy endings.

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:32.720
We'll have to wait until Frozen II premieres
on November 22 to find out for sure.

